## PR previews

`preview.yml` builds apps on every PR with no secrets; `preview-deploy.yml` (environment `preview`)
uploads the result as version `pr-<n>` of `<app>-preview`. Store `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and
`CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` only as secrets of the `preview` environment (and of the prod deploy
environment), with Deployment branches set to Selected, `main`; never as repository secrets, which
every PR workflow could read.

## Update bot

`splice.yml` runs the weekly `splice update` in every CI mode. Create the environment `splice-bot`
first (Deployment branches = Selected, `main`) and keep its credentials only there, never as
repository secrets. It also refreshes `pnpm-lock.yaml`; after resolving a conflict PR run
`pnpm install --lockfile-only` and push.

A PR opened with `github.token` gets no CI and cannot change workflows. Pick a token, in order:

1. GitHub App with Contents, Pull requests and Workflows write: variable `SPLICE_APP_CLIENT_ID`,
   secret `SPLICE_APP_KEY` (in `splice-bot`).
2. PAT (same permissions): environment secret `SPLICE_BOT_TOKEN`.
3. Session mode: repository variable `SPLICE_BOT=off` skips the job; an agent runs
   `splice update --all` on a branch and opens the PR (workflow files need the workflow scope).
